      },
      "message": "fix(app): drilling reads the stock the setup's earlier operations left\n\nThe axial drill's reach (#84), R-plane (#91) and holder laws read the\nstock top over each disk as min(raw stock, prior surface): #96's\nPriorPlan (the setup's stock grid cut by every earlier op's cached\nmoves), read at the highest covered cell; unknown, ungenerated or\nposed predecessors leave the raw stock. The plan is simulated lazily,\nonly when the raw reading refuses, and shared with verify's #96\nacquittal. A lathe axial drill reads the grid revolved about the axis,\nand turning predecessors are cut as their nose ball. Cross drills keep\nthe raw stock (the column grid cannot be read along a radial line).\nThe Drill stamp carries the ahead-ops digest, so a drill judged against\nan earlier pocket goes Stale when that pocket's path moves.\n\nFixes #89\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
