      "message": "fix(app): drill prior credits only lathe facing, cones drill predecessors\n\nPR #123 review fixes:\n- B1/B2: on a lathe the prior plan credits only the Facing kind cut\n  with its nose ball; a boring bar, groove or parting blade ahead (cut\n  as a full disc and revolved, or a column credited under standing\n  material) makes the prior unknown - the raw stock stands.\n- A twist-drill predecessor is cut with its point cone (as Taper),\n  so a pilot's 118 deg point is not read as a flat floor.\n- The turning nose radius joins the rest digest.\n- Every Drill stamps the stock it read, so an axial drill goes Stale\n  on a stock change.\n- cut_by keeps a NaN raw height NaN (the non-finite law).\n- Nits: the prior disk is padded by half a cell diagonal, an over-long\n  ring count is refused instead of clamped, vertical-plane arcs are\n  dropped from the nose-lowered path.\n\nTests: drill_prior_kinds (boring ahead on a lathe refused, pilot cone\nrefuses R 6, axial drill Stale on stock change), drill_prior (parting\nahead does not credit the end face, R 0.1 under the faced end refused).\n\nRefs #89\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
