      "message": "fix(app): a turning kind ahead on a mill-turn is not credited either - only nose-cut Facing is\n\nThe #89 review fix gated the facing-only rule on the Lathe machine kind,\nso a mill-turn still credited a boring/grooving/parting op ahead of an\naxial drill through the column grid. The rule now holds on any machine\nfor turning-family kinds (and for every kind on a lathe). Pinned by\ndrill_prior_kinds::a_turned_boring_op_ahead_of_a_mill_turn_axial_drill_is_not_credited\n(fails without this change).\n\nRefs #89\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
